[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Managed LLM Platforms (Part 2 of 3)","textKn":"ನಿರ್ವಹಿತ LLM ವೇದಿಕೆಗಳು (ಭಾಗ 2 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 2 of 3: a two-provider gateway on a virtual clock with capability and sensitivity routing, retries with exponential backoff and jitter, errors that are not retried, a circuit breaker timeline, retry amplification over 1000 requests, a total deadline, a tool call that may already have run and the request cost formula. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind managed LLM platforms (request latency and TTFT, percentiles, an M/M/1 queue, the break-even of a reservation, a two-provider gateway with capability and sensitivity routing, retries with backoff, a circuit breaker, deadlines, the duplicate-execution problem, percentile dashboards, request-level cost attribution, log redaction, fallback evaluation and a readiness check), not the real software, and the providers are simulators with scripted or seeded failures on a virtual clock, the latencies, prices, bills, usage records and evaluation counts are simulated or invented by the lab, no Bedrock, Azure OpenAI or Vertex AI call is made and nothing says a configuration is compliant, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied and the lesson code was shown only in part, so the labs are our own implementation and the outputs were produced by running them. Parts 2 and 3 of the pasted lesson are cut off: Part 2 stops in section 11.4 on Bedrock attribution, so the Azure subscription and resource-group attribution, the Vertex AI project-per-team billing, the BigQuery billing-export analysis and the comparator walkthrough are missing, and Part 3 stops in section 14.2 on Vertex attribution and its code listing ends after the enumerations, so the Azure attribution, the production checklist, the final exercise and the quiz are missing. The checklist in the third lab is therefore our own teaching list. The lesson figures of about 50 ms against 75 ms TTFT, the 40 to 60 percent break-even band, the 21 to 50 dollars per hour range and every statement about Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Vertex AI, PTUs, Gemini, IAM, BAA or HIPAA are cited and were not checked or measured here. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 2ನೆಯದು: ವರ್ಚುವಲ್ ಗಡಿಯಾರದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮತೆ ರೂಟಿಂಗ್ ಇರುವ ಎರಡು-ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರ gateway, ಘಾತೀಯ backoff ಮತ್ತು jitter ಜೊತೆ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ, ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನಿಸದ ದೋಷಗಳು, circuit breaker ಸಮಯರೇಖೆ, 1000 ವಿನಂತಿಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ ವರ್ಧನೆ, ಒಟ್ಟು ಗಡುವು, ಈಗಾಗಲೇ ಓಡಿರಬಹುದಾದ ಸಾಧನ ಕರೆ ಮತ್ತು ವಿನಂತಿ ವೆಚ್ಚ ಸೂತ್ರ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು ನಿರ್ವಹಿತ LLM ವೇದಿಕೆಗಳು (ವಿನಂತಿ ವಿಳಂಬ ಮತ್ತು TTFT, ಶತಮಾನಾಂಶಗಳು, M/M/1 ಸರದಿ, ಮೀಸಲಿನ ಸಮಭಾರ ಬಿಂದು, ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮತೆ ರೂಟಿಂಗ್ ಇರುವ ಎರಡು-ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರ gateway, backoff ಜೊತೆ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ, circuit breaker, ಗಡುವುಗಳು, ನಕಲು-ಕಾರ್ಯಗತಗೊಳಿಕೆ ಸಮಸ್ಯೆ, ಶತಮಾನಾಂಶ ಡ್ಯಾಶ್‌ಬೋರ್ಡ್, ವಿನಂತಿ-ಮಟ್ಟದ ವೆಚ್ಚ ಹಂಚಿಕೆ, ಲಾಗ್ ಮರೆಮಾಚುವಿಕೆ, fallback ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಮತ್ತು ಸಿದ್ಧತೆ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರರು ವರ್ಚುವಲ್ ಗಡಿಯಾರದಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ಅಥವಾ seeded ವೈಫಲ್ಯಗಳಿರುವ ಸಿಮ್ಯುಲೇಟರ್‌ಗಳು, ವಿಳಂಬ, ಬೆಲೆ, ಬಿಲ್, ಬಳಕೆ ದಾಖಲೆ ಮತ್ತು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಎಣಿಕೆಗಳನ್ನು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಅನುಕರಿಸಿದೆ ಅಥವಾ ಕಲ್ಪಿಸಿದೆ, ಯಾವುದೇ Bedrock, Azure OpenAI ಅಥವಾ Vertex AI ಕರೆ ಮಾಡಿಲ್ಲ ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವುದೇ ಸಂರಚನೆ ಅನುಸರಣೆಯದ್ದು ಎಂದು ಏನೂ ಹೇಳುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ ಮತ್ತು lesson ಕೋಡ್ ಭಾಗಶಃ ಮಾತ್ರ ತೋರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ ಮತ್ತು ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಅನ್ನು ಅವನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿ ಪಡೆಯಲಾಗಿದೆ. ಅಂಟಿಸಿದ lesson ನ ಭಾಗ 2 ಮತ್ತು 3 ಕತ್ತರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿವೆ: ಭಾಗ 2 ವಿಭಾಗ 11.4 ರಲ್ಲಿ Bedrock ಹಂಚಿಕೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತದೆ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ Azure subscription ಮತ್ತು resource-group ಹಂಚಿಕೆ, Vertex AI project-per-team ಬಿಲ್ಲಿಂಗ್, BigQuery billing-export ವಿಶ್ಲೇಷಣೆ ಮತ್ತು comparator ವಿವರಣೆ ಕಾಣೆಯಾಗಿವೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಭಾಗ 3 ವಿಭಾಗ 14.2 ರಲ್ಲಿ Vertex ಹಂಚಿಕೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ಕೋಡ್ ಪಟ್ಟಿ enumerations ನಂತರ ಮುಗಿಯುತ್ತದೆ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ Azure ಹಂಚಿಕೆ, ಉತ್ಪಾದನಾ ಪರಿಶೀಲನಾ ಪಟ್ಟಿ, ಅಂತಿಮ ಅಭ್ಯಾಸ ಮತ್ತು ರಸಪ್ರಶ್ನೆ ಕಾಣೆಯಾಗಿವೆ. ಮೂರನೇ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ನ ಪರಿಶೀಲನಾ ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಬೋಧನಾ ಪಟ್ಟಿ. ಸುಮಾರು 50 ms ವಿರುದ್ಧ 75 ms TTFT, 40 ರಿಂದ 60 ಶೇಕಡಾ ಸಮಭಾರ ಬ್ಯಾಂಡ್, ಗಂಟೆಗೆ 21 ರಿಂದ 50 ಡಾಲರ್ ವ್ಯಾಪ್ತಿ ಮತ್ತು Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Vertex AI, PTU, Gemini, IAM, BAA ಅಥವಾ HIPAA ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಪ್ರತಿ ಹೇಳಿಕೆ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿತ ಮತ್ತು ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿಲ್ಲ ಅಥವಾ ಅಳೆಯಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Available Is Not the Same as Allowed","textKn":"ಲಭ್ಯ ಎಂದರೆ ಅನುಮತಿಸಿದ್ದು ಅಲ್ಲ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"A Two-Provider Gateway on a Virtual Clock","headingKn":"ವರ್ಚುವಲ್ ಗಡಿಯಾರದಲ್ಲಿ ಎರಡು-ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರ Gateway","bodyEn":"The lesson original gateway code was cut off, so this part builds a gateway of its own and runs it against simulated providers. It checks that a provider has the capabilities a request needs and is approved for its data class before calling it, retries retryable errors with exponential backoff and jitter inside a total deadline, never retries an invalid request, opens a circuit breaker after consecutive failures and probes it after a cooldown, and falls back to a second provider. It then measures retry amplification over 1000 requests, shows a refund that ran twice when a timeout was ambiguous, and prices a request. Time is a virtual clock that nothing waits on.","bodyKn":"lesson ನ ಮೂಲ gateway ಕೋಡ್ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತ್ತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಈ ಭಾಗ ತನ್ನದೇ gateway ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಸಿಮ್ಯುಲೇಟೆಡ್ ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರರ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರನನ್ನು ಕರೆಯುವ ಮೊದಲು ಅವನಿಗೆ ವಿನಂತಿಗೆ ಬೇಕಾದ ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯಗಳಿವೆ ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ವರ್ಗಕ್ಕೆ ಅನುಮೋದಿತ ಎಂದು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನಿಸಬಹುದಾದ ದೋಷಗಳನ್ನು ಒಟ್ಟು ಗಡುವಿನೊಳಗೆ ಘಾತೀಯ backoff ಮತ್ತು jitter ಜೊತೆ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಅಮಾನ್ಯ ವಿನಂತಿಯನ್ನು ಎಂದಿಗೂ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಸತತ ವೈಫಲ್ಯಗಳ ನಂತರ circuit breaker ತೆರೆದು ಕೂಲ್‌ಡೌನ್ ನಂತರ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಎರಡನೇ ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರನಿಗೆ ಹಿಂತಿರುಗುತ್ತದೆ. ನಂತರ 1000 ವಿನಂತಿಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ ವರ್ಧನೆ ಅಳೆಯುತ್ತದೆ, ಟೈಮ್‌ಔಟ್ ಅಸ್ಪಷ್ಟವಾದಾಗ ಎರಡು ಬಾರಿ ಓಡಿದ ಮರುಪಾವತಿ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ವಿನಂತಿಗೆ ಬೆಲೆ ಕಟ್ಟುತ್ತದೆ. ಸಮಯ ಯಾವುದೂ ಕಾಯದ ವರ್ಚುವಲ್ ಗಡಿಯಾರ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"The Gateway","headingKn":"Gateway","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">a fallback must be eligible, not just available</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">policy</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">capability and data class</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">route</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">primary then secondary</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">retry</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">backoff and a cap</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">breaker</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">stop calling a sick provider</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">a fallback must be eligible, not just available</text></svg>","captionEn":"Eligibility, retries, a breaker and a deadline decide which provider answers.","captionKn":"ಅರ್ಹತೆ, ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ, breaker ಮತ್ತು ಗಡುವು ಯಾವ ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The gateway decisions","headingKn":"Gateway ನಿರ್ಧಾರಗಳು","headers":["Situation","Decision in the lab"],"rows":[["request needs image input","skip the primary, use the secondary"],["restricted data, no approved provider","refuse"],["rate limit or temporary error","retry with 200 ms, 400 ms backoff and jitter"],["invalid request","raise at once, no retry, no fallback"],["authentication failure","no retry, move to the secondary"],["3 consecutive failures","open the breaker, probe after 5000 ms"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"mp_2.py","headingEn":"Providers, breaker and gateway","headingKn":"ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರರು, breaker ಮತ್ತು gateway","descEn":"Gateway.eligible checks capability and sensitivity, Gateway.generate walks the providers with a deadline, retries and backoff, Breaker tracks closed, open and half-open and Effects deduplicates a side effect only when it is given a key.","descKn":"Gateway.eligible ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮತೆ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, Gateway.generate ಗಡುವು, ಮರುಪ್ರಯತ್ನ ಮತ್ತು backoff ಜೊತೆ ಪೂರೈಕೆದಾರರ ಮೂಲಕ ನಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ, Breaker closed, open ಮತ್ತು half-open ಟ್ರ್ಯಾಕ್ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು Effects key ನೀಡಿದಾಗ ಮಾತ್ರ ಅಡ್ಡ ಪರಿಣಾಮ ನಕಲು ತೆಗೆಯುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"class Sens(Enum):
    PUBLIC = 0
    INTERNAL = 1
    CONFIDENTIAL = 2
    RESTRICTED = 3


class Err(Enum):
    RATE_LIMIT = "rate_limit"
    TEMPORARY = "temporary"
    UNAVAILABLE = "unavailable"
    INVALID = "invalid_request"
    AUTH = "authentication"
    TIMEOUT_AFTER_EFFECT = "timeout_after_effect"


RETRYABLE = {Err.RATE_LIMIT, Err.TEMPORARY, Err.UNAVAILABLE, Err.TIMEOUT_AFTER_EFFECT}


class ProviderError(Exception):
    def __init__(self, kind):
        super().__init__(kind.value)
        self.kind = kind


class Clock:
    def __init__(self):
        self.ms = 0.0

    def advance(self, d):
        self.ms += d


@dataclass
class Request:
    request_id: str
    task: str
    sensitivity: Sens
    capabilities: frozenset
    budget_ms: int = 5000
    allow_fallback: bool = True
    team: str = "support"
    side_effect: str = ""


@dataclass
class Config:
    name: str
    model: str
    capabilities: frozenset
    max_sensitivity: Sens
    p_in: float
    p_out: float
    latency_ms: int


class Provider:
    def __init__(self, cfg, clock, script=None, failure_rate=0.0, seed=0, effects=None):
        self.cfg, self.clock, self.script = cfg, clock, list(script or [])
        self.failure_rate, self.rng, self.calls, self.effects = failure_rate, random.Random(seed), 0, effects

    def generate(self, req, idem_key=None):
        self.calls += 1
        self.clock.advance(self.cfg.latency_ms)
        err = self.script.pop(0) if self.script else (Err.UNAVAILABLE if self.rng.random() < self.failure_rate else None)
        if err is not None:
            if err == Err.TIMEOUT_AFTER_EFFECT and self.effects is not None and req.side_effect:
                self.effects.run(req.side_effect, idem_key)
            raise ProviderError(err)
        if self.effects is not None and req.side_effect:
            self.effects.run(req.side_effect, idem_key)
        return {"provider": self.cfg.name, "model": self.cfg.model, "input_tokens": 1200, "output_tokens": 300}


class Effects:
    """The external side effect, for example a payment. With a key it deduplicates, without one it repeats."""

    def __init__(self):
        self.done, self.count = set(), 0

    def run(self, name, key):
        if key is not None and (name, key) in self.done:
            return
        self.done.add((name, key))
        self.count += 1


class Breaker:
    def __init__(self, clock, threshold=3, recovery_ms=5000):
        self.clock, self.threshold, self.recovery_ms = clock, threshold, recovery_ms
        self.state, self.fails, self.opened_at = "closed", 0, 0.0

    def allow(self):
        if self.state == "open":
            if self.clock.ms - self.opened_at >= self.recovery_ms:
                self.state = "half_open"
                return True
            return False
        return True

    def success(self):
        self.state, self.fails = "closed", 0

    def failure(self):
        self.fails += 1
        if self.state == "half_open" or self.fails >= self.threshold:
            self.state, self.opened_at = "open", self.clock.ms


class Gateway:
    def __init__(self, primary, secondary, clock, max_attempts=3, use_breaker=True, seed=1):
        self.providers = [primary, secondary]
        self.clock, self.max_attempts = clock, max_attempts
        self.breakers = {p.cfg.name: Breaker(clock) for p in self.providers} if use_breaker else {}
        self.rng, self.log = random.Random(seed), []

    @staticmethod
    def eligible(cfg, req):
        if not req.capabilities <= cfg.capabilities:
            return False, "missing capability " + ",".join(sorted(req.capabilities - cfg.capabilities))
        if req.sensitivity.value > cfg.max_sensitivity.value:
            return False, f"not approved for {req.sensitivity.name.lower()} data"
        return True, "ok"

    def generate(self, req, idempotent=True):
        deadline = self.clock.ms + req.budget_ms
        order = self.providers if req.allow_fallback else self.providers[:1]
        for prov in order:
            ok, why = self.eligible(prov.cfg, req)
            if not ok:
                self.log.append((req.request_id, prov.cfg.name, "skipped", why))
                continue
            br = self.breakers.get(prov.cfg.name)
            if br and not br.allow():
                self.log.append((req.request_id, prov.cfg.name, "skipped", "circuit open"))
                continue
            for attempt in range(self.max_attempts):
                if self.clock.ms + prov.cfg.latency_ms > deadline:
                    self.log.append((req.request_id, prov.cfg.name, "stopped", "deadline"))
                    raise TimeoutError("deadline exceeded")
                try:
                    res = prov.generate(req, req.request_id if idempotent else None)
                    if br:
                        br.success()
                    self.log.append((req.request_id, prov.cfg.name, "ok", f"attempt {attempt + 1}"))
                    res["fallback_used"] = prov is not order[0]
                    return res
                except ProviderError as e:
                    self.log.append((req.request_id, prov.cfg.name, "error", e.kind.value))
                    if e.kind == Err.INVALID:
                        raise
                    if e.kind == Err.AUTH:
                        break
                    if br:
                        br.failure()
                    if e.kind not in RETRYABLE or attempt == self.max_attempts - 1 or (br and br.state == "open"):
                        break
                    back = min(200 * 2 ** attempt, 1000) * self.rng.uniform(0.8, 1.2)
                    if self.clock.ms + back + prov.cfg.latency_ms > deadline:
                        self.log.append((req.request_id, prov.cfg.name, "stopped", "deadline"))
                        raise TimeoutError("deadline exceeded")
                    self.clock.advance(back)
        raise RuntimeError("no provider could serve the request")


BEDROCK = Config("bedrock", "model-b", frozenset({"text", "json", "tools"}), Sens.CONFIDENTIAL, 3.0, 15.0, 800)
AZURE = Config("azure", "model-a", frozenset({"text", "json", "tools", "image"}), Sens.CONFIDENTIAL, 2.5, 10.0, 700)


def cost(cfg, tin, tout):
    return tin / 1e6 * cfg.p_in + tout / 1e6 * cfg.p_out


def make(script_b=None, script_a=None, fr_b=0.0, fr_a=0.0, **kw):
    clock = Clock()
    eff = Effects()
    b = Provider(BEDROCK, clock, script_b, fr_b, 1, eff)
    a = Provider(AZURE, clock, script_a, fr_a, 2, eff)
    return clock, b, a, eff, Gateway(b, a, clock, **kw)"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"mp_2.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() runs eight experiments on the simulated gateway.","descKn":"main() ಸಿಮ್ಯುಲೇಟೆಡ್ gateway ಮೇಲೆ ಎಂಟು ಪ್ರಯೋಗ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely running: routing by capability and sensitivity")
    reqs = [Request("r1", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"})), Request("r2", "extract", Sens.CONFIDENTIAL, frozenset({"text", "json"})),
            Request("r3", "image analysis", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text", "image"})), Request("r4", "regulated", Sens.RESTRICTED, frozenset({"text"}))]
    clock, b, a, eff, gw = make()
    for r in reqs:
        try:
            res = gw.generate(r)
            print(f"{r.task:15} -> {res['provider']} (fallback used: {res['fallback_used']})")
        except RuntimeError as e:
            print(f"{r.task:15} -> refused: {e}")
    for entry in gw.log:
        if entry[2] == "skipped":
            print("   skipped:", entry[1], "-", entry[3], "for", entry[0])
    print("the plain summary and the extraction went to the primary, the image request skipped it for lacking image input and went to the secondary without any failure, and the restricted request was refused because neither simulated provider is approved for it; routing here is by a label and a capability set, which is a simplification of a real data-governance decision")

    section("2. Genuinely running: retries with exponential backoff and jitter")
    clock, b, a, eff, gw = make(script_b=[Err.RATE_LIMIT, Err.RATE_LIMIT])
    res = gw.generate(Request("r5", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"})))
    print("log:", [(e[1], e[2], e[3]) for e in gw.log])
    print(f"served by {res['provider']} after {b.calls} primary calls | virtual time used {clock.ms:.0f} ms | base delays 200, 400 ms with plus or minus 20 percent jitter")
    print("the first two attempts were rate limited, the gateway waited about 200 ms and then about 400 ms and the third attempt succeeded on the same provider without any fallback, and the total time of roughly 3 seconds is three provider latencies of 800 ms plus the two waits; the clock is virtual and nothing slept")

    section("3. Genuinely running: errors that should not be retried")
    for kind in (Err.INVALID, Err.AUTH):
        clock, b, a, eff, gw = make(script_b=[kind, kind, kind])
        try:
            res = gw.generate(Request("r6", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"})))
            out = f"served by {res['provider']}"
        except ProviderError as e:
            out = f"raised {e.kind.value}"
        print(f"{kind.value:16} primary calls {b.calls} | secondary calls {a.calls} | {out}")
    print("an invalid request was sent once and surfaced as an error, because repeating it or sending it to another provider would only repeat the mistake, while an authentication failure on the primary was not retried and moved to the secondary, since the fault is that provider's configuration; this is the lab's policy choice and a real policy should follow each provider's documented error semantics")

    section("4. Genuinely running: a circuit breaker over time")
    clock, b, a, eff, gw = make(script_b=[Err.UNAVAILABLE] * 4)
    print(f"{'t (ms)':>8} {'breaker':>10} {'primary calls':>14} {'served by':>10}")
    print(f"{clock.ms:>8.0f} {gw.breakers['bedrock'].state:>10} {b.calls:>14} {'-':>10}   before any request")
    for i in range(1, 7):
        res = gw.generate(Request(f"c{i}", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"})))
        print(f"{clock.ms:>8.0f} {gw.breakers['bedrock'].state:>10} {b.calls:>14} {res['provider']:>10}")
    clock.advance(6000)
    res = gw.generate(Request("c7", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"})))
    print(f"{clock.ms:>8.0f} {gw.breakers['bedrock'].state:>10} {b.calls:>14} {res['provider']:>10}   after 6000 ms: a half-open probe failed")
    clock.advance(6000)
    res = gw.generate(Request("c8", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"})))
    print(f"{clock.ms:>8.0f} {gw.breakers['bedrock'].state:>10} {b.calls:>14} {res['provider']:>10}   after another 6000 ms: the probe succeeded")
    print("the three attempts of the very first request were enough to open the breaker, the next five requests went straight to the secondary and the primary call count stayed at 3, the first probe after the cooldown failed and reopened it, and the next probe succeeded, closed the breaker and was served by the primary again; this breaker lives in one process and a fleet of gateways would each have its own")

    section("5. Genuinely measuring: retry amplification over 1000 requests")
    for label, br in (("no breaker", False), ("with breaker", True)):
        clock, b, a, eff, gw = make(fr_b=0.5, fr_a=0.0, use_breaker=br)
        served = Counter()
        for i in range(1000):
            clock.advance(10)
            r = Request(f"a{i}", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"}), allow_fallback=False)
            try:
                gw.generate(r)
                served["ok"] += 1
            except (RuntimeError, TimeoutError):
                served["failed"] += 1
        print(f"{label:13} logical requests 1000 | provider attempts {b.calls} | per request {b.calls / 1000:.2f} | succeeded {served['ok']}")
    print("with half the attempts failing and up to three attempts per request the primary received 1717 attempts for 1000 requests, close to the expected 1 plus 0.5 plus 0.25 per request, and 888 succeeded against an expected 875; with the breaker the primary received only 26 attempts and 11 requests succeeded, because the breaker kept it closed off for most of the 10 virtual seconds and the other requests failed immediately, since this run has no fallback; retries multiply load, a breaker removes that load, and without a second provider the cost of removing it is failed requests")

    section("6. Genuinely running: a total deadline")
    clock, b, a, eff, gw = make(script_b=[Err.TEMPORARY] * 6)
    try:
        gw.generate(Request("d1", "summarise", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"}), budget_ms=1500, allow_fallback=False))
    except TimeoutError as e:
        print("raised:", e, "| primary calls", b.calls, "| virtual time", f"{clock.ms:.0f} ms", "| budget 1500 ms")
    print("with a 1500 ms budget and 800 ms per attempt the gateway made one attempt, saw that waiting and trying again could not finish inside the budget, and stopped instead of spending time on a doomed retry; a budget has to cover every attempt together and not each one separately")

    section("7. Genuinely running: a tool call that may already have happened")
    for label, idem in (("no idempotency key", False), ("same key on both providers", True)):
        clock, b, a, eff, gw = make(script_b=[Err.TIMEOUT_AFTER_EFFECT])
        gw.generate(Request("pay-1", "refund", Sens.INTERNAL, frozenset({"text"}), side_effect="refund-order-77"), idempotent=idem)
        print(f"{label:28} side effects executed: {eff.count}")
    print("the primary carried out the refund and then the connection timed out, so the gateway could not tell and tried the secondary; without a key the refund ran twice and with one key shared across providers it ran once, which is why model calls and external side effects have to be separated and the effect made idempotent")

    section("8. Genuinely computing: the cost of one request")
    for cfg in (BEDROCK, AZURE):
        print(f"{cfg.name:8} 1200 input and 300 output tokens at {cfg.p_in} and {cfg.p_out} per million: {cost(cfg, 1200, 300):.6f}")
    print("the cost is input tokens over a million times the input price plus output tokens over a million times the output price, and it comes to 0.0081 for the first provider and 0.006 for the second with these invented prices; real bills add charges for caching, batch, images and reserved capacity")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
